Searching has its own penalty, though - it takes turns.  Early
characters for whom food is a problem may find the cost of exhaustive
searching too great for the small chance of stepping on a trap.  You
also may want to run rather than search if there's a monster
approaching.  So there's a trade-off involved.

Taking notes has no penalties (other than your own patience) - it takes
0 turns.  Restoring the discoveries list from said notes doesn't simply
make the deliberate call to forget_objects() less effective - it reduces
it to an interface inconvenience.


